Yumcarta - Privacy Policy

Last updated: 23 November 2026

Yumcarta is a mobile street-food cooking game made by CodingTech Studio, Başakşehir / İstanbul, Türkiye ("we").
Contact: codingtechstudio@gmail.com

Yumcarta is made for adults. It is not directed to children and we do not knowingly collect data from children.


1. What stays on your device

Your progress, coins, gems, stars, stalls, staff, branches, boosters and settings are stored only on your device. We have no account system and no server of our own. Deleting the game deletes this data.


2. Ads

The game shows ads through Google AdMob: videos you choose to watch for a reward (more tips, twenty more seconds, a life, double coins from a branch's till or a free booster) and full-screen ads after some result screens. There is no banner. To show and measure ads, Google receives the advertising identifier of your device, your IP address (from which an approximate location is derived), device information and your interactions with the ads.

In the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland, a consent form from Google asks for your choice before any ad is requested. Elsewhere the game asks with its own window ("Allow" / "Don't allow"). Without your consent to personalised ads, only non-personalised ads are requested. You can reopen your choice at any time under Settings > Privacy. You can also reset or delete the advertising identifier in your device settings.

"Remove ads" in the shop turns off the full-screen ads; videos for rewards stay available if you want them.

How Google uses data from apps that use its services: https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites


3. Play statistics

Outside the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland, and only if you choose "Allow" in the game's own privacy window, the game sends play statistics through Google Analytics for Firebase: which shift was started, won or lost, what was bought with coins or gems, which reward videos were watched, and similar events. They carry no name, e-mail address or free text. Google links them to an app-instance identifier created for this installation, and receives device information and your IP address (used for the country, not stored with the events). We use these statistics only to balance and improve the game. Event and user data are deleted after 14 months. If you do not allow it, nothing is sent. In the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland the game sends no play statistics at all.


4. Purchases

If you buy something in the shop, the payment is handled entirely by Google Play (or the App Store). We never see your card or payment details. The game only learns from the store which product was bought and keeps the transaction identifier on your device so that a product is delivered once. "Restore purchases" in the shop asks the store again which one-time products your store account owns.


5. Who receives data

Google Ireland Limited / Google LLC, as the provider of AdMob, Google Analytics for Firebase and Google Play billing. Google may process data on servers outside your country, including the United States; it relies on the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework and standard contractual clauses. We do not sell your data and we share it with no one else.


6. How long data is kept

Data on your device: until you delete the game or its data. Play statistics: 14 months. Ad data is kept by Google under its own policies.


7. Your rights

Depending on where you live (for example under the GDPR, the UK GDPR or the Turkish Law No. 6698, KVKK), you have the right to ask what data is held about you, to have it corrected or deleted, to object to or restrict its use, to withdraw your consent at any time, and to complain to your data protection authority. You can change your choice in the game under Settings > Privacy at any time: after "Don't allow" no further play statistics are sent, and what was sent before is deleted after 14 months at the latest. You can reset your advertising identifier in your device settings. With any question or request, write to codingtechstudio@gmail.com. We answer within 30 days.


8. Permissions

Internet access and network state (ads, play statistics, purchases), the advertising identifier (ads), billing (purchases through Google Play) and vibration (short feedback pulses you can switch off in Settings).


9. Changes

If this policy changes, the date at the top changes and the new text is published at the same address.


